.\" ctt-digup -- semantic file search CLI (DigUp via MCP / mcp2cli)
.\" Man page for the ctt-digup project (https://github.com/rikkooo/ctt-digup)
.TH CTT-DIGUP 1 "October 2026" "ctt-digup 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctt-digup \- semantic file search for every agent and every shell (DigUp via MCP and mcp2cli)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctt-digup
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ]
.PP
.B ctt-digup search
.IR query ...
.RB [ \-n
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-kind
.IR K,K ]
.RB [ \-\-code ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B ctt-digup index
.IR folder ...
.RB [ \-\-code ]
.PP
.B ctt-digup estimate
.IR folder ...
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B ctt-digup status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B ctt-digup download\-model
.PP
.B digup
.IR command ...
.RB [ \-\-index
.IR DIR ]
.PP
.B mcp2cli
.RB [ @digup ]
.IR tool
.RI [ tool\-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctt-digup
makes DigUp's on\-device semantic file search available from bash, from scripts,
and from any MCP\-capable agent on Windows 11 and WSL Ubuntu\-26.04.
DigUp (https://github.com/ARahim3/DigUp) finds files by
.I meaning
with Google DeepMind's EmbeddingGemma 2: describe what you are looking for in
your own words and it returns the matching PDF page, photo, video moment,
audio minute, document passage or line of code.
.PP
Nothing you index leaves your computer. The model runs locally (llama.cpp);
the only network use is the one\-time model download and DigUp's optional daily
update check.
.PP
.B ctt-digup
is a thin wrapper that exposes the DigUp MCP server as ordinary commands via
.BR mcp2cli (1)
(\fB@tronsfey/mcp2cli\fR). The same operations are reachable three ways:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B ctt-digup
\(em friendly subcommands (\fBsearch\fR, \fBindex\fR, \fBestimate\fR, \fBstatus\fR, \fBdownload\-model\fR) for shells and scripts
.IP \(bu 2
.B digup
\(em the native DigUp developer CLI, with the full flag set
.IP \(bu 2
.B mcp2cli
\(em the raw MCP tool names (\fBdigup_search\fR, \fBdigup_index\fR, \fBdigup_estimate\fR, \fBdigup_status\fR, \fBdigup_download_model\fR) for agent integration
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.SS ctt-digup commands
.TP
.B ctt-digup search \fIquery...\fR [\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-kind\fR \fIK,K\fR] [\fB\-\-code\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Search the index by meaning (and by exact words). \fIquery\fR is one or more words;
quote multi\-word phrases. \fB\-n\fR/\fB\-\-limit\fR sets how many hits to return
(default 10). \fB\-\-kind\fR filters to a comma\-separated list of
\fBscreenshot\fR, \fBimage\fR, \fBpdf\fR, \fBdoc\fR, \fBaudio\fR, \fBvideo\fR.
\fB\-\-code\fR (or a query starting with \fBcode:\fR) searches the code index.
\fB\-\-json\fR prints a JSON array of hits (see \fBOUTPUT\fR).
.TP
.B ctt-digup index \fIfolder...\fR [\fB\-\-code\fR]
Sync the index with the given folders: embed what is new, then the rest of long
PDFs and documents. \fB\-\-code\fR also builds the code index (source files, the
repos' docs and notebooks, minus what git ignores).
.TP
.B ctt-digup estimate \fIfolder...\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Report what would be indexed and how long the first pass takes on this machine,
per folder. Always run this before a large first index.
.TP
.B ctt-digup status [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show what is in the index: path of the index database, vector and segment counts,
per\-kind file counts, and index size.
.TP
.B ctt-digup download\-model
Download (or resume downloading) the EmbeddingGemma 2 model files (~865 MB).
Run once before indexing or searching.
.TP
.B ctt-digup list\-tools
List the MCP tools exposed by the DigUp server (mcp2cli \fB\-\-list\fR).
.TP
.B ctt-digup help
Print the wrapper's help text, the tool mapping and examples.
.SS digup native commands
These are the DigUp developer CLI subcommands. \fBctt-digup\fR maps onto them;
use \fBdigup\fR directly when you need the full flag set.
.TP
.B digup estimate \fIfolder...\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
What would be indexed, and how long the first pass takes.
.TP
.B digup index \fIfolder...\fR [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-code\fR] [\fB\-\-reindex\fR]
Sync the index with these folders and embed what is new.
\fB\-\-limit\fR caps the number of files in this pass; \fB\-\-reindex\fR drops
vectors and embeds everything again (after a settings or model change).
.TP
.B digup search \fIwords...\fR [\fB\-\-kind\fR \fIK,K\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Search by meaning. A query starting with \fBcode:\fR searches the code index,
e.g. \fBdigup search "code: retry a failed call with backoff"\fR.
.TP
.B digup status
What is in the index (authoritative index location).
.TP
.B digup download\-model [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Fetch the model files, with resume, checked (JSON lines progress).
.TP
.B digup speed [\fB\-\-model\fR]
This machine's speed next to the M4 Pro behind the estimates, and what indexing
has measured here.
.SS mcp2cli tool mapping
.B ctt-digup
is backed by the DigUp MCP server (\fBsrc/mcp-server/index.js\fR) through
.BR mcp2cli .
Each MCP tool becomes a CLI command:
.PP
.RS
.nf
MCP tool              ctt-digup / mcp2cli call          digup native
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
digup_search          ctt-digup search ...              digup search ...
digup_index           ctt-digup index ...               digup index ...
digup_estimate        ctt-digup estimate ...            digup estimate ...
digup_status          ctt-digup status                  digup status
digup_download_model  ctt-digup download-model          digup download-model
.fi
.RE
.PP
Raw tool calls (for agents and scripts) use mcp2cli's tool\-name form:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mcp2cli @digup --list
mcp2cli @digup digup_status
mcp2cli @digup digup_search --query "zebra in a video" --limit 5
mcp2cli @digup digup_search --input-json '{"query":"invoice","limit":3}' --json
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Search and index options
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR
Return at most \fIN\fR hits (search; default 10) or index at most \fIN\fR files
in this pass (index).
.TP
.BI \-\-kind " K,K"
Restrict to file kinds: \fBscreenshot\fR, \fBimage\fR, \fBpdf\fR, \fBdoc\fR,
\fBaudio\fR, \fBvideo\fR. Comma\-separated. For example
\fB\-\-kind pdf,doc\fR finds the lease clause and skips photos.
.TP
.B \-\-code
Estimate, index or search the code index (\fBcode.sqlite\fR in the index
folder): source files, their repos' docs and notebooks, minus what git ignores.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-code
Also index loose source code and data files as documents (outside code projects).
.TP
.B \-\-include\-datasets
Do not skip folders that look like datasets.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " DIR"
Do not index this folder (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-ext " EXT"
Do not index files with this extension (repeatable, or comma\-separated:
\fB\-\-exclude\-ext heic,txt\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-reindex
Drop vectors and embed everything again (after changing settings or model).
.SS Index location
.TP
.BI \-\-index " DIR"
Use \fIDIR\fR as the index folder instead of DigUp's default Application
Support folder. Keep separate corpora apart with separate index folders, e.g.
\fB\-\-index ~/indexes/windows\fR vs \fB\-\-index ~/indexes/wsl\fR.
.SS Output and mcp2cli options
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable JSON output (search: an array of hits; estimate: one JSON
object per folder; status: a JSON object).
.TP
.B \-\-input\-json \fIjson\fR
Pass tool arguments to an mcp2cli tool call as a JSON object.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Raw JSON output from mcp2cli (no pretty\-printing).
.TP
.BI \-\-jq " expression"
Filter mcp2cli output with a JMESPath expression.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List available MCP tools and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-describe " tool"
Show a tool's schema (parameters, types, descriptions).
.SS Ranking options (digup native)
.TP
.BI \-\-zgate " Z"
How far a meaning match must stand out (default 2.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-word\-weight " W"
Bonus for containing all of the query's words (default 2.0).
.SH OUTPUT
.B ctt-digup search \-\-json
prints a JSON array. Each hit has at least \fBpath\fR, \fBkind\fR,
\fBsegment\fR, \fBsegment_id\fR, \fBscore\fR, \fBmodified\fR, \fBsize\fR and
\fBinfo\fR, and when they apply \fBz\fR (how far the best segment stands out),
\fBcosine\fR, \fBkeyword_rank\fR, \fBloc\fR / \fBloc_end\fR (PDF page, or seconds
into audio/video, or the code stretch), \fBfocus\fR (code line to open at) and
\fBexcerpt\fR (a short text snippet):
.PP
.RS
.nf
[
  {
    "excerpt" : "...tenant may keep one pet with written consent...",
    "info" : { "pages" : "24" },
    "kind" : "pdf",
    "loc" : 7,
    "path" : "/mnt/c/Users/enric/Documents/lease.pdf",
    "score" : 12.4,
    "segment" : "page",
    "segment_id" : 412,
    "size" : 184320,
    "z" : 3.1
  }
]
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Download the model once (resumes if interrupted):
.PP
.RS
.nf
digup download-model
.fi
.RE
.TP
Estimate, then index the Windows user folders from WSL:
.PP
.RS
.nf
digup estimate /mnt/c/Users/enric/Documents /mnt/c/Users/enric/Desktop \\
               /mnt/c/Users/enric/Downloads
digup index    /mnt/c/Users/enric/Documents /mnt/c/Users/enric/Desktop \\
               /mnt/c/Users/enric/Downloads
.fi
.RE
.TP
Index WSL folders with the code index on:
.PP
.RS
.nf
digup index ~/devs --code
.fi
.RE
.TP
Find the pets clause in a lease (semantic search):
.PP
.RS
.nf
ctt-digup search "the clause about pets in the lease" --kind pdf
.fi
.RE
.TP
Find the moment a zebra shows up in a video, JSON out:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ctt-digup search "zebra in a video" --kind video --json
.fi
.RE
.TP
Find a function by what it does (code index):
.PP
.RS
.nf
digup search "code: retry a failed call with backoff"
.fi
.RE
.TP
Search one corpus only, with a dedicated index folder:
.PP
.RS
.nf
digup search "invoice from last March" --index ~/indexes/windows --json
.fi
.RE
.TP
Check index health and size:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ctt-digup status
digup status --index ~/indexes/wsl
.fi
.RE
.TP
Call the same tool through mcp2cli (agent style):
.PP
.RS
.nf
mcp2cli @digup digup_search --query "payment declined error" --limit 5
mcp2cli @digup digup_status --json
.fi
.RE
.TP
Pipe hits into jq and open the first path:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ctt-digup search "invoice from last March" --json \\
  | jq -r '.[0].path' | xargs xdg-open
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DIGUP_BIN
Path to the \fBdigup\fR binary used by the MCP server and the \fBctt-digup\fR
wrapper. Default: \fB/usr/local/bin/digup\fR on Linux/WSL. Set it when digup
lives elsewhere, e.g. \fBDIGUP_BIN=/usr/lib/DigUp/helper/digup\fR.
.TP
.B DIGUP_MODELS
Directory that holds the EmbeddingGemma 2 model files. When set, digup looks
for the model
.I only
there; otherwise it uses DigUp's Application Support folder or the Hugging Face
cache. Share one download across index folders with
\fBDIGUP_MODELS=~/.local/share/digup/Models\fR.
.TP
.B DIGUP_WORKER_DIR
Set to \fBworker\fR to use the mlx\-lm reference worker instead of llama.cpp
(evals only).
.TP
.B MANPATH
Include the directory holding \fBctt-digup.1\fR (or install it into
\fB/usr/local/share/man/man1\fR) so \fBman ctt-digup\fR resolves.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/digup/index/index.sqlite
Default main vector + keyword index on Linux and WSL (see \fBdigup status\fR
for the authoritative path). Windows: under \fB%LOCALAPPDATA%\fR (DigUp's data
folder). macOS: \fB~/Library/Application Support/DigUp/\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/digup/index/code.sqlite
Code index (built with \fB\-\-code\fR), kept separate from document search.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/digup/Models/
Default model folder on Linux/WSL (override with \fBDIGUP_MODELS\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/digup/index/costs.json
What indexing has measured on this machine (used by \fBestimate\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.mcp2cli/bakes.json
mcp2cli saved server shortcuts (the \fB@digup\fR bake).
.TP
.I mcp.json
MCP server registration (command, args, \fBDIGUP_BIN\fR); see
\fIdocs/MANUAL.md\fR chapter "MCP integration".
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/ctt-digup.1
Install location for this man page:
\fBsudo cp man/ctt-digup.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success;
.B 1
on usage or runtime errors (e.g. searching before any folder is indexed, or a
missing model);
.B 2
on invalid arguments.
